---
import StandardsLayout from "../../components/StandardsLayout.astro";
import CitationBlock from "../../components/CitationBlock.astro";
import ScholarlyMeta from "../../components/ScholarlyMeta.astro";
import SectionBlock from "../../components/SectionBlock.astro";
import { derivePublicationMetadata } from "../../utils/publication";

const pageTitle = "Citing the standards in contracts and audits";
const pageDescription =
  "How to write Ethotechnics standards into contracts, procurement language, and audits. This is guidance: it adds no requirements and is not legal advice.";
const permalink = "/standards/where-this-binds";
const anchorLinks = [
  { href: "#language", label: "Sample language" },
  { href: "#records", label: "Records to request" },
  { href: "#audits", label: "Audit checks" },
  { href: "#citations", label: "Citations" },
];

const publication = derivePublicationMetadata({
  permalink,
  published: "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z",
  updated: "2026-10-06T00:00:00Z",
  version: "v1.2.0",
  authorName: "Ethotechnics Institute",
  changelogSummary:
    "Named the record to request for each clause in the sample, with its evidence pack, in place of generic advice on validator results; only STD-01 §7.1 has a scoring tool. Pinned the current versions: STD-07 v0.1.3, STD-08 v0.3.1, STD-01 v1.0.2, and STD-02 v1.4, whose §8.4 no longer scales standing to exposure.",
});

// What to ask the supplier for under each clause of the sample. The record is
// what the clause's own text names; the pack is where the standard lists its
// evidence. STD-07 has no evidence pack yet, so its row points at the article.
const clauseRecords = [
  {
    clause: "STD-07 §4.2",
    record:
      "Every objection record accepted on the declared channel, paired with the revision or reasoned-refusal record that answered it. The time between the two should fall inside the reversal clock declared in contest.reversal_clock.",
    source: {
      label: "STD-07, Article IV",
      href: "/standards/std-07-revisable-delegation-record#articles",
    },
  },
  {
    clause: "STD-08 §1.1 and §1.2",
    record:
      "For each renewal in the term: the grant's renewal_basis, dated before the review period began, and the renewal record naming what was examined, what would have been visible had the grant been failing, and who looked.",
    source: { label: "STD-08 evidence pack", href: "/evidence-packs/std-08" },
  },
  {
    clause: "STD-08 §1.3",
    record:
      "The grant's scope at issue and today. For every widening, the evidence_basis and correction-capacity check made for it, and its entry in the grant's state_history.",
    source: { label: "STD-08 evidence pack", href: "/evidence-packs/std-08" },
  },
  {
    clause: "STD-01 §7.1",
    record:
      "The published burden report and the time-cost log it was computed from.",
    source: {
      label: "STD-01 evidence pack",
      href: "/evidence-packs/std-01#std-01-7-1",
    },
  },
  {
    clause: "STD-02 §8.4",
    record:
      "The standing register entry for the decision class: who_may_challenge, naming both affected_party and corrective_labor, and the response_deadline. Then the case log of operators' challenges, with when each was answered.",
    source: {
      label: "STD-02 evidence pack",
      href: "/evidence-packs/std-02#std-02-8-4",
    },
  },
];
---

<StandardsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  permalink={permalink}
  seoTitle={`${pageTitle} — Standards`}
  anchorLinks={anchorLinks}
  publishedTime="2025-06-01T00:00:00.000Z"
  modifiedTime="2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"
  mainClass="page page--wide"
>
  <SectionBlock
    id="language"
    eyebrow="Sample language"
    title="A starting clause"
    description="It binds four obligations: an answer to every objection, authority renewed only on evidence, a published time cost, and standing for the people a decision falls on and the staff who repair its errors. Adapt it with counsel to your jurisdiction."
  >
    <pre
      class="binding-clause">
Supplier will meet the following clauses of the Ethotechnics Institute standards, at the versions named, for the system described in Schedule A.

- STD-07 v0.1.3 §4.2: every objection accepted on the declared channel produces a revision or a reasoned refusal, on the record, within the stated reversal clock.
- STD-08 v0.3.1 §1.1 to §1.3: the system's grant of authority states in advance the evidence its renewal requires; a renewal that rests only on the absence of observed failure is not a renewal; and any widening of the grant's scope is a new authorization with its own evidence.
- STD-01 v1.0.2 §7.1: Supplier measures and publishes the time the system costs the people it decides about.
- STD-02 v1.4 §8.4: standing extends to the people a decision falls on and to the operators who handle its exceptions, work its queues, and do its manual repair. Each is owed receipt of a challenge, an answer within the same response deadline, and a decision against the published standard.

Supplier will provide the records each clause names on request. These standards are drafts; the versions above are fixed for the term of this agreement.
    </pre>
  </SectionBlock>

  <SectionBlock
    id="records"
    eyebrow="Records to request"
    title="The record behind each clause"
    description="The sample obliges the supplier to produce these on request. Each row names the record and where the standard lists its evidence."
    variant="alt"
  >
    <div class="mapping-table__wrapper">
      <table class="mapping-table mapping-table--stack">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Clause</th>
            <th scope="col">Record to request</th>
            <th scope="col">Evidence listed in</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            clauseRecords.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{row.clause}</th>
                <td data-label="Record to request">{row.record}</td>
                <td data-label="Evidence listed in">
                  <a href={row.source.href}>{row.source.label}</a>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">
      Of these five, only STD-01 §7.1 has a scoring tool on this site. The <a
        href="/validators/burden-modeler">Burden Modeler</a
      > scores one user journey red at over 25 minutes, more than 7 steps, or a screen
      with no exit. A contract can require a remediation plan for any journey that
      scores red. The other clauses have no score; the record is the evidence.
    </p>
  </SectionBlock>

  <SectionBlock
    id="audits"
    eyebrow="Audits"
    title="What an auditor checks against those records"
  >
    <ul>
      <li>
        STD-07 §4.2: sample objections. Each answer was recorded inside the
        reversal clock of the record it answers.
      </li>
      <li>
        STD-08 §1.1 and §1.2: sample renewals. Each renewal_basis predates its
        review period, and no renewal rests on the absence of failure alone.
      </li>
      <li>
        STD-08 §1.3: compare the grant's scope at issue with its scope today.
        Every widening has its own evidence and its own entry in state_history.
      </li>
      <li>
        STD-01 §7.1: recompute the published time cost from the time-cost log.
      </li>
      <li>
        STD-02 §8.4: find the staff who handle exceptions under
        who_may_challenge, and check their challenges were answered within the
        response_deadline.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </SectionBlock>

  <SectionBlock
    id="citations"
    eyebrow="Citations"
    title="Reference this guidance"
    description="Cite the canonical permalink and version, so the governance document points at a fixed text."
    variant="alt"
  >
    <ScholarlyMeta publication={publication} permalink={permalink} />
    <CitationBlock
      title={pageTitle}
      permalink={permalink}
      publication={publication}
    />
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--space-5)">
      See also: <a href="/standards">Standards</a> &middot; <a
        href="/standards/enforceable-governance-crosswalks"
        >Framework map for buyers and auditors</a
      >
    </p>
  </SectionBlock>
</StandardsLayout>

<style>
  /* A contract clause is read, not scanned like code: wrap it to the column
     instead of scrolling it sideways, and keep the first line clear of the
     copy button. */
  .binding-clause {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    padding-top: var(--space-7);
  }
</style>
